      "id": "ctx-paper",
      "kind": "context",
      "status": "verified",
      "content": "[PAPER] 6a = (R,R,S)-Pga-Pro-Aib-pTxa-OMe, C31H34N4O7S, <750 Da. N-terminal pyroglutamic acid binds lactam substrates by two H-bonds; the C-terminal pTxa thioxanthone absorbs visible light and sensitises by triplet energy transfer. NMR (33 ROE restraints, 233 K, CD2Cl2, Xplor-NIH; 10-structure bundle, heavy-atom r.m.s.d. 0.22 A) gives a type II' beta-turn with a pTxa NH...O=C Pga H-bond and the thioxanthone above the turn.",
      "tags": [
        "6a-structures"
