    {
      "id": "ctx-target",
      "kind": "context",
      "status": "verified",
      "content": "[PAPER] Experimental target: E_T(6a) = 269 kJ/mol, from the inflection point of the 77 K phosphorescence spectrum in EtOH (Fig. 2, main text; FluoroMax-4P, 0.1 ms delay). Longest-wavelength absorption 383 nm, epsilon 5,700 M-1 cm-1 (EtOH). The paper attributes both to the thioxanthone in pTxa and calls them comparable to parent 9H-thioxanthen-9-one (ref. 36, Nikitas et al., Org. Biomol. Chem. 19, 5237 (2021)). The paper gives no photophysical data for other catalysts or substrates. [AI conversion] 269 kJ/mol = 2.788 eV; 383 nm = 3.24 eV.",
      "tags": [
        "6a-structures",
        "6a-triplet"
      ],
      "references": [],
      "evidence": [
