      "id": "fail-srun",
      "kind": "failed_attempt",
      "status": "verified",
      "content": "[TOOL] Launching BigDFT with srun on this cluster fails: OpenMPI 5 needs PMIx, Slurm offers only pmi2, so srun starts N independent single-process copies ('12 singletons'), which overwrite each other's logs and run out of memory (first Phase 1 submission, cancelled after 42 s, no results). Use mpirun -np $SLURM_NTASKS --map-by slot:PE=$OMP_NUM_THREADS inside the Slurm allocation, and check 'Number of MPI tasks' in the log at start-up.",
